cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workflow, please cite this repository and the corresponding thesis or associated publication when available."

title: "Turrialba Fresh-Cheese Shotgun Metagenomics Workflow"

type: software

authors:
  - given-names: "Randall"
    family-names: "Bonilla-Sandoval"

version: "1.0.0"

date-released: "2026-10-06"

abstract: >-
  Reproducible computational workflow for shotgun metagenomic
  characterization of fresh cheese produced in Santa Cruz de Turrialba,
  Costa Rica. The workflow includes preprocessing, bovine host-read
  depletion, producer-level coassembly, multi-binner MAG reconstruction,
  MAG quality control and dereplication, functional annotation,
  genome-resolved ecology, bacteriocin-oriented analyses, resistome,
  virome, mobilome, virulence-associated screening, 16S rRNA loci
  recovered from shotgun assemblies, read-level taxonomic profiling,
  and targeted validation of selected pathogen-associated taxonomic
  signals.

keywords:
  - shotgun metagenomics
  - fresh cheese
  - metagenome-assembled genomes
  - MAGs
  - microbiota
  - bacteriocins
  - lactic acid bacteria
  - food microbiology
  - Turrialba
  - Costa Rica

license: MIT

repository-code: "https://github.com/Duquecaos/Turrialba_Fresh_Cheese_Metagenomics"
